\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Are almost nonnegatively curved manifolds rationally elliptic; do they admit Riemannian metrics with vanishing topological entropy; do nonnegatively curved manifolds have nonnegative Euler characteristic; and are positively curved manifolds formal?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2011/18}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Are almost nonnegatively curved manifolds rationally elliptic; do they admit Riemannian metrics with vanishing topological entropy; do nonnegatively curved manifolds have nonnegative Euler characteristic; and are positively curved manifolds formal?

